# Proof / provenance / compliance rule

> `.cursor/rules/do-not-touch.mdc` (alwaysApply) is the floor. This rule sits **on top** of it —
> never below. If they conflict, do-not-touch wins.

## Read first

- `docs/PROOF_COMPLIANCE_CONTEXT.md` — provenance vocabulary + honesty contract
- `docs/DO_NOT_TOUCH.md` — locked surfaces
- `ADR-006` — testnet-only gate, audit-before-mainnet

## Must avoid

- Mislabeling provenance as `live` / `attested` when the source is weaker (Estimated / Manual / Stale).
- Making `isAttestorAllowlisted` fail-**open** — unknown attestor must return `false`.
- Relabeling Base Sepolia (testnet) data as mainnet.
- Removing the testnet notice from any proof surface.

## Validate before done

- `pnpm test` for the touched area:
  `por-summary-truth`, `proof-card-onchain-provenance`, `output-guard`, `forbidden-words`.
- Panel badge = **weakest** row (worst provenance wins, never the best).
- Demo path is **always simulated**: sentinel hashes only, never presented as real on-chain proof.

## STOP and ask before

- Editing `config/deployments.base-sepolia.json`.
- Loosening `canRunDemoProvider()` (`src/lib/demo/guard.ts`).
- `latestAttestationVerified` is **duplicated** in BOTH
  `src/app/(product)/proof-center/page.tsx` AND `src/app/admin/proof-center/page.tsx` —
  change both or neither.

## Priority

P1
